  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 203 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nA few remnant showers and possibly a thunderstorm will pass through \nnorthern portions of the area this morning; however, there should be \na diminishing trend through sunrise.\n\nThe ridge that has been in place across the area the past few days \nwill gradually build back across the area today; however, another \nMCS is expected to slide around the periphery of the ridge this \nafternoon. The latest trends would have this staying just north of \nthe CWA, across northern IL this afternoon before diving southeast \nthrough central IN to southwest OH this evening. It may brush close \nenough to touch off storms over southwest IN, but the chances look \npretty slim overall. Kept a 20-30% chance up near the Evansville Tri-\nState area, with mainly dry conditions elsewhere as the ridge builds \nback into the area from the southwest. In fact, the SPC has kept the \nsouthwest IN and adjacent portions of KY/IL in a Marginal Risk of \nsevere weather today with the main threat being damaging winds if \nstorms happen to pass through that area.\n\nThe ridge will continue to expand and intensify across the area for \nthe end of the week into the weekend, which will allow temperatures \nto climb along with the humidity. The Extreme Heat Warning as kept \nin place and unchanged from the previous forecast update with heat \nindex values expected to be in the 105-115 degree range through the \nweekend! This will be a dangerous and prolonged period of extreme \nheat.\n\nA frontal boundary is progged to sag southward into the area for \nMonday, which may briefly bring slightly cooler temperatures (upper \n80s to low 90s) for Tuesday into Wednesday of next week. At this \npoint, any break in the heat would be great!!",
